# Rationale: The linchpin patch (docs/tdd/01-chromium-engine.md §3). Parses the
#   signed per-profile FingerprintConfig in the BROWSER process BEFORE the first
#   script runs, verifies its signature against the Manager's public key, and
#   propagates a minimized per-renderer view to every renderer and worker process
#   so values are present before Blink initializes script — closing the V3
#   cross-context leak by construction. Everything in layer1 reads from the
#   accessor this patch introduces. Fails closed on an unsigned/invalid config.
# Surface: config ingest / signature verify / IPC propagation (all fingerprint surfaces depend on it)
# Threat-vectors: enables V1/V2/V3 defenses; the mechanism for ADR 0006 (one binary, N identities)
# Upstream-risk: HIGH. Touches process startup (//chrome/browser), RenderProcessHost
#   init (//content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc), a new
#   //third_party/blink/renderer/core/fingerprint module, and the worker bootstrap
#   in //third_party/blink/renderer/platform. Upstream refactors of process init or
#   the Mojo bootstrap will conflict here; this patch is the tracking bot's
#   highest-attention item.
# Tests: v3-traces/cross-context-consistency, v1-coherence/* (all depend on config being present pre-script)
# Target-milestone: M1
# Status: BACKLOG
#
# --- Implementation plan (M1) ------------------------------------------------
# 1. //chrome/browser startup:
#      * parse a new switch --proteus-fingerprint-config=<path> and env
#        PROTEUS_LAUNCH_NONCE.
#      * read the file, canonicalize, verify Ed25519 signature against the
#        Manager public key baked into the build (or provided via secure channel).
#      * on failure: LOG(FATAL) — fail closed. Never launch with an unverified
#        identity (Principle VI-adjacent; docs/adr/0006).
# 2. Parse into an immutable browser-process FingerprintConfig struct; derive a
#    minimized per-renderer view (a renderer needs its surfaces, not sidecar hints).
# 3. Add a FingerprintConfig mojom; deliver the serialized view at
#    RenderProcessHost init so it is present before Blink script init. Workers
#    inherit from their creating renderer through the existing worker bootstrap.
# 4. Add blink::FingerprintConfig accessor (thread-safe, immutable). Surface code
#    (patches 0002+) queries it. No global mutable state, no late injection.
#
# This file is intentionally a valid, reviewable M1 backlog specification. Its
# git-format patch payload will be generated against the pinned baseline during
# M1 implementation.
